 "Here are a thousand mobile money transfers, sent across Kenya, Ghana and Uganda. Five of them, in red, are fraud.": "275e019777.mp3",
 "A fraud alarm checks every transfer. It catches ninety-five percent of frauds, and wrongly flags three percent of honest transfers. The flagged ones rise up.": "03ac9381ad.mp3",
 "Gather every flagged transfer into the tray. Five are fraud. About thirty are honest people, flagged by mistake, simply because honest transfers are so many.": "83ae2abc4d.mp3",
 "So when the alarm goes off, fraud is only about one chance in seven. That is Bayes' theorem: what you believed before, multiplied by how well the evidence fits.": "f7e401ffc5.mp3",
 "Now check the flagged ones again with a second, independent test, such as calling the customer. Most false alarms fall away. Yesterday's answer becomes today's starting point.": "6076ae9e27.mp3",
 "Where fraud is common, the same alarm is far more often right. The rarer the thing you look for, the more false alarms you must expect.": "86f3b82b70.mp3"
